-- title:
--   Existence of tame-fixed admissible small constants over A
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime with $q \ge 5$, let $M'$ be a nonzero natural number not divisible by $q$, and let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` lying over $q$, in the sense that the image of $q$ belongs to the set of nonunits of $A$. The assertion is that there are an intermediate field $k_0$ of $\mathbb Q \subseteq \overline{\mathbb Q}$ and an element $\pi_0$ of $k_0$ whose image in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lies in $A$ such that, writing $A_0$ for the pullback of $A$ along $k_0 \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb Q}$ (that is, $A \cap k_0$): $A_0$ is a discrete valuation ring whose maximal ideal is generated by $\pi_0$; $A_0$ is a henselian local ring; the residue field of $A_0$ is algebraically closed; every $a \in A$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to some $c \in k_0 \cap A$; every $\mathbb Q$-automorphism $\tau$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $x \in A \iff \tau x \in A$ for all $x$ maps $k_0$ into itself; and for every $\pi \in A$ with $\pi^{q^2-1} = q$ and every $\tau$ in `A.inertiaSubgroupIn ℚ` (the image in $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)$ of the inertia subgroup of the decomposition subgroup of $A$) whose tame character value $A.\mathrm{tameCharacter}\,\pi\,\tau$ — the residue in the residue field of $A$ of $\tau\pi/\pi$ when that quotient lies in $A$, and $0$ otherwise — equals $1$, the automorphism $\tau$ fixes every element of $k_0$. Moreover there is a prime $\ell$ with $\ell \ge 3$, $\ell \ne q$ and $\ell \nmid M'$, an element $\zeta_0$ of $k_0$ which is a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, and an element $\varpi_t$ of $k_0$ lying in $A$ with $\varpi_t^{q^2-1} = q\,u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$.
--
--   This provides the base field of "small constants" for the local analysis at $q$: a countable, decomposition-stable subfield $k_0$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ whose intersection with $A$ is a henselian discrete valuation ring with algebraically closed residue field surjecting onto that of $A$, carrying a $q\ell$-th root of unity and a $(q^2-1)$-st root of $q$ up to a unit, and fixed pointwise by those tame inertia elements on which the tame character is trivial. It is used in the construction of supersingular charts and node presentations on modular curves of full level, where the least layer of the tower is required to satisfy exactly these conditions.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ValuationSubring_exists_admissible_smallConstants_tameFixed.lean

